@page "/security"
@layout Paycrest.Components.Layout.PublicLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]
@inject IConfiguration Config

<PageTitle>Security · WageHarbor</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="How WageHarbor protects payroll data: encrypted SSNs and bank numbers, separate data for every company, role-based access, two-step sign-in and an audit log." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.wageharbor.com/security" />
</HeadContent>

<article class="prose">
    <h1>How we protect your payroll data</h1>
    <p class="prose-sub">Payroll holds some of the most sensitive information a business has. Here's how WageHarbor looks after it.</p>

    <h2>Every company's data is kept separate</h2>
    <p>Each company on WageHarbor has its own private space. Every request is limited to the signed-in person's company at the data layer, and changes to another company's records are refused. People at one company can never see another company's employees, pay or settings.</p>

    <h2>Sensitive numbers are encrypted</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Social Security numbers and bank account numbers are <strong>encrypted at rest</strong> and shown masked (for example ***-**-4354 or ••••1712).</li>
        <li>Viewing a full Social Security number is recorded in the audit log.</li>
        <li>Passwords are never stored. Only a salted, one-way hash is kept, using ASP.NET Core Identity.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The right people see the right things</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Roles</strong> (Admin, HR, Payroll, Manager and Employee) decide who can see and change what.</li>
        <li>Employees only ever see their own pay, time and details.</li>
        <li>Admins can reset passwords and <strong>disable sign-in</strong> immediately when someone leaves.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Strong sign-in</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Two-step sign-in</strong> with an authenticator app, plus recovery codes.</li>
        <li><strong>Passkeys</strong> for password-free sign-in on supported devices.</li>
        <li>Sessions are re-checked every 30 minutes, so someone whose sign-in is disabled is signed out of any open session within that time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>A record of every change</h2>
    <p>The audit log records who changed company settings, employee records, pay setup, payroll runs and tax tables, and when, so mistakes and misuse can be traced.</p>

    <h2>Your part</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Turn on two-step sign-in for everyone with the Admin or Payroll role.</li>
        <li>Give each person the smallest role they need.</li>
        <li>Share temporary passwords privately, never in group chats or email threads.</li>
        <li>Disable sign-in for people who leave, on their last day.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Report a security concern</h2>
    <p>If you think you've found a security problem, please email <a href="mailto:@ContactEmail">@ContactEmail</a> with the details. We take every report seriously.</p>
</article>

@code {
    private string ContactEmail => Config["Site:ContactEmail"] is { Length: > 0 } e ? e : "contact@wageharbor.com";
}
